to rtl/, no `cores/<target>/` prefix.\\n    description: "What you\\\'ll change in this file."\\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv          # Or `test/test_<name>.py` for cocotb suites.\\n    description: "..."\\n```\\n\\n### Common mistakes that make schemas reject the file (do NOT do these)\\n\\n- `expected_impact: "free-text description"` — schema requires an OBJECT with `fitness_delta_pct` (integer) and `confidence` (enum). Strings are rejected.\\n- `expected_impact: {fitness_delta_pct: 5.0, confidence: "Med"}` — `fitness_delta_pct` must be a Python integer (not float, not "5"); `confidence` must be lowercase `low`/`medium`/`high`.\\n- `changes[i].file: cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv` — schema\\\'s regex requires the `rtl/...` form. Drop the `cores/<target>/` prefix.\\n- `changes[i].file: alu.sv` — the regex requires the `rtl/` prefix.\\n- Writing the YAML inline in your message instead of using the write tool.\\n\\nUse the write tool now.\']\' returned non-zero exit status 1.\n\nMotivation:\n(none)\n\nHypothesis:\n(none)\n\nExpected impact:\n(none)\n\nImplementation notes (the implementing agent\'s self-report):\n(no notes)\n\nRTL diff (cores/bench/rtl/) — what was actually changed:\n```\n(no diff captured)\n```\n\n## Your job\n\nAppend at most ONE bullet to cores/bench/LESSONS.md, in this format:\n\n  - YYYY-MM-DD <id> (<outcome>, <delta_pct>): <one-sentence lesson>\n\nA useful lesson:\n  - Captures *why* the outcome happened, not just *what* happened.\n  - Generalizes to future iterations (a pattern, gotcha, or design constraint),\n    not a one-off bug.\n  - Names specific RTL constructs / hazards / CoreMark behaviors when relevant.\n\nExamples of GOOD lessons (do not copy verbatim — write your own):\n  - "Dual-issue without a 2W register file creates WAW hazards riscv-formal\'s\n    \'reg\' check catches; reg file must expose two write ports."\n  - "64-entry BHT regressed CoreMark; the always-not-taken default was already\n    well-tuned to this benchmark\'s branch profile